plan Streams
title   Streams
status  proposed
goal
    Own continuing external values through named stream declarations with latest-value projection,
    exact completion, and one release. Preserve terminal truth without replaying emissions.
    This proposed Plan is pending approval. It establishes no shipped implementation claim.
outcomes
    O1  Exact stream families expose continuing value and terminal truth
        The exact stream API below fixes descriptor authoring, exact methods, closed state/value
        unions, field optionality, and typed outcomes. Preserve P/K/V/E/R through descriptor, named
        O, machine, app, Runtime, fixture, and Story. Identity/key validation uses
        @plan.Resources.O1 and its inline canonical-key rules. Runtime capabilities remain outside
        P; service requirements remain inferred R. Stream types capture no parent selector,
        routed event, or child actor.

        stream(config) constructs an inert descriptor with these accepted authoring fields:

        | Field | Required | Accepted relationship |
        | --- | --- | --- |
        | id | Yes | Exact authored descriptor ID |
        | key | Yes | (params:P) => K, synchronously |
        | subscribe | Yes | subscribe(params:P, { signal }); exact return remains @Q1 |
        | persist | No | boolean; omitted means false |

        subscribe receives the supported AbortSignal. Preserve exact P/K/V/E/R without deciding
        whether the final adapter directly returns Stream or an Effect producing Stream. @Q1 owns
        that missing return relationship and the caller-written mapper container.

        Key/getState and construction of an unreturned plan are passive. A stream is an actor-owned
        continuing operation, not a canonical resource-store entry. It has no actor cancel, getData,
        public occurrence handle, generic stream registry, or cross-actor deduplication. Missing
        reads return idle without ownership, work, mutation, or history invention.

        States distinguish idle, running, complete, typed failure, defect, and interrupted. The
        hasValue discriminator determines exact latest/count presence. Complete and interruption
        remain distinct; a no-value terminal state is valid.

        StreamFamily<P, K extends unknown[], V, E> has exactly these methods:

        | Method | Exact signature |
        | --- | --- |
        | key | (params: P): K |
        | getState | (key: K): StreamState<V,E,K> |
        | subscribe | (p:P,options?:StreamSubscriptionOptions<P,K,V,E>):ContinuingOperationPlan |

        StreamValue<V> is the exact closed union below. No other latest/count presence is accepted.

        | hasValue | Exact fields |
        | --- | --- |
        | false | latest?:never; emissionCount:0. |
        | true | latest:V; emissionCount:number. |

        StreamState<V,E,K> is the exact closed union below. Every lane has key:K and intersects
        StreamValue<V>. Fields absent from a lane remain absent.

        | status | Other exact fields |
        | --- | --- |
        | idle | generation:null. |
        | running | generation:number. |
        | complete | generation:number. |
        | failure | generation:number; error:E. |
        | defect | generation:number; defect:unknown. |
        | interrupted | generation:number. |

        No-value state has no latest field and has count zero. Value state has exact V and a safe
        non-negative emission count. Generation is null only in idle; admitted generations begin at
        one. Absent fields remain absent. Complete, typed failure, defect, and interruption are
        distinct.

        Subscription options map value(V), complete(), failure(E), defect(), and interrupt() to one
        exact machine event. The failure mapper is unavailable
        when E is never. Mappers receive no Exit, Cause, state, or lifecycle. Widened completion
        values reject. Complete Cause classification belongs to @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O2.
        The mapper names and arguments are fixed. Their direct-member versus outcomes container
        remains unresolved at @Q1; an illustrative example cannot select it.

        The [stream example](references/data-api.examples.ts) illustrates the descriptor form.

        `persist` defaults false. True retains only accepted latest, terminal, generation,
        declaration, key, and ownership facts for an independently persistable stable actor. It
        never persists an executable stream. The family has no actor cancel or getData method. The
        named options and plan aliases describe semantic roles and add no public exports.

    O2  Continuing declaration identity controls acquisition, projection, and release
        Only state activities and independent onMemory declarations under @plan.Statecharts.O4 own
        continuing streams. Binding identity is compiled declaration slot, operation kind, exact
        descriptor, and K. Activation generation is monotonic metadata; P is retained input, never
        identity. Equal normalized identity retains generation and original P. Changed identity
        releases old once before replacement. False/null/exit/replacement/disposal finalizes the
        declaration exactly once. Declaration slots remain private.

        A second distinct live declaration by the same actor for the same descriptor/K rejects
        before replacing or releasing existing work. The retained same declaration is not a
        duplicate. Different actors remain independent even for equal descriptor/K. Register
        cancellation/fencing before any scheduler can execute work. Finalizers release once in
        reverse acquisition order. Planned close/release has no mapped outcome and never calls an
        authored interruption mapper. Normal remote completion, typed failure, defect, interruption,
        and release failure retain distinct evidence. Cleanup defects record issues without rolling
        back an already published transition. Actor suspension, resume barriers, cleanup quarantine,
        and disposal obey @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O5.

        Each emission updates latest value, hasValue, emissionCount, and declaration generation in
        the current projection. Emissions create no finite occurrences. Slow projection readers may
        skip intermediate values and observe the current latest snapshot. Adjacent projection-only
        updates may coalesce; terminal and mapped-event facts retain their boundaries. There is no
        emission history or replay promise. App-authored dropping/coalescing belongs in the stream
        program; Flow supplies no pressure options.

        Projection-only publication evaluates no transition, guard, action, redirect, memory patch,
        finite work, or hidden event. Authored mapped events enter later ordinary turns under
        @plan.Statecharts.O3. Emissions change durable machine state only through those events or
        explicit authoritative resource writes under @plan.Resources.O4. Values never become
        canonical resource data implicitly.

        Match actor incarnation, declaration slot, descriptor/K, and generation immediately before
        emission or terminal publication. Released/stale generation emissions and finalizers cannot
        affect replacement work, current projection, later actor incarnations, or mapped events.
        Complete/failure/defect/interruption settles terminal truth once. Retained terminal streams
        never restart implicitly. Safe-integer admission/restore reserves terminal publication and
        cleanup headroom; count/generation exhaustion fails before partial publication or reuse.
    O3  Persistence retains a projection without serializing a running stream
        Persist defaults false. True opts in only accepted declaration/key/generation/ownership,
        latest-value/count, and terminal facts for an independently durable stable actor under
        @plan.Persistence.O2. Fibers, scopes, cursors, transports, buffered emissions, programs, and
        history are never persistable. A stream never makes its actor durable implicitly.

        Hydration retains exact latest/hasValue/count/terminal truth without emission replay. After
        pending mapped outcomes drain, an active live declaration rematerializes from complete
        executable P in a new generation under @plan.Persistence.O4. K cannot reconstruct input or a
        transport session. Missing P fails closed with a precise diagnostic and invents no history.
        Terminal streams do not restart. Restored generation fences suppress facts from former
        sessions. Reconciliation never admits a finite lookup or commit.
decisions
    D1  Streams own sessions rather than shared resource entries
        Descriptor/K identifies an actor declaration's stream projection. Equal-key actors retain
        independent sessions. Named families expose latest and terminal truth without a registry.
    D2  Latest projection does not imply history or durable machine state
        Readers observe current snapshots and may skip values. Mapped events and explicit writes
        separately own durable changes. Restoring projection does not replay or resume a session.
constraints
    C1  Keep continuing work bounded by declarations
        Add no runtime-sized subscribeMany/subscribeEach, manual unsubscribe handle, stream cancel,
        public declaration/occurrence handle, child actor/activity equivalent, hidden lifetime
        registry, cross-actor deduplication, terminal restart, or key-to-input inversion.
    C2  Keep release and execution boundaries explicit
        Planned release is cleanup and has no mapped domain outcome. Behaviorally visible phased
        remote work requires an explicitly owned AppPlan actor. An operational lease may remain
        scoped inside a stream; it creates no public lifetime or cancellation channel.
verification
    V1  Exact API and state inference
        Establish @O1. Planned, unbuilt checks:
        `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/stream-types.test.ts` and
        `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/stream.test.ts`. Compile exact P/K/V/E/R,
        value/completion/error mapping, all status lanes, generation null only in idle, and latest
        absence when hasValue false. Reject widened completion values, E=never failure mapping,
        parent-type capture, cancel/getData/registry methods, wrong K/P, and Cause access. Passive
        missing reads and unreturned plans must start no work. Compile required id/key/subscribe
        and optional persist; reject unknown fields and mismatched P/K/V/E/R. Exact adapter return
        and wrong mapper-container proofs remain blocked by @Q1.
    V2  Session identity, latest projection, and release races
        Establish @O2. Planned, unbuilt check:
        `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/stream-lifecycle.test.ts`. Test equal
        declaration retention and changed slot/kind/descriptor/K replacement. Add a duplicate
        same-actor declaration while existing work runs; pass when it rejects without disturbing
        existing work. Equal keys in another actor must remain independent.

        Emit zero/one/many values, delay a reader, complete/fail/defect/interrupt, and release via
        false/null/exit/suspend/dispose. Pass when latest/count/generation/terminal fields are
        exact, slow readers may skip values, terminal facts settle once, and finalizers run once.
        Planned release calls no outcome mapper. Mapped events remain later ordinary turns, and
        emissions alone change no machine memory or canonical data. Race late
        emission/terminal/finalizer against replacement, incarnation, and exhausted counters; no
        stale publication is allowed.
    V3  Durable projection and fresh-session hydration
        Establish @O3. Planned, unbuilt check:
        `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/operation/test/stream-hydration.test.ts`. Capture
        no-value/value/running/terminal streams on durable and non-durable owners. Pass when only
        declared durable facts survive, pending outcomes drain first, and active streams start from
        live P in a new fenced generation. Preserve latest/count without replaying values,
        transports, or finite work. Terminal streams must start no adapter; missing P must fail
        closed with owned path/code diagnostics. Cover former-session late emissions and explicit
        resource writes separately through @plan.Resources.V4.
questions
    Q1  Which stream adapter return and mapper container are accepted?
        The sources fix subscribe(P,{signal}), exact P/K/V/E/R, and the named outcome mappers.
        They do not settle a direct Stream versus Effect-producing-Stream adapter return, or direct
        mapper members versus an outcomes object. Keep both exact forms unresolved; import no
        legacy routes, done mapper, pressure options, or parent callback arguments.
